  "summary": "A full-duplex 12-bit SDR built on an AD9363 transceiver and a Xilinx Zynq SoC, sold by Analog Devices as a teaching tool. Guaranteed for 325 MHz to 3.8 GHz with 20 MHz of bandwidth, it is widely reconfigured in software to report as the higher-grade AD9364 and open up 70 MHz to 6 GHz with 56 MHz of bandwidth.",
