   "risk_level": "high",
   "notes": "Higher risk than most things in this batch, because the device's normal operation is unauthorised access. Brute-forcing logins and copying files from systems you do not own violates the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act in the US, the Computer Misuse Act in the UK, and equivalents elsewhere - and because it runs autonomously, 'I only meant to scan' is not much of a defence once it has authenticated to something. Use it on an isolated lab network you built, or under a written engagement scope. This is not legal advice."
