  "honest_take": "This module adds no RFID capability of its own - every read/write/emulate/attack capability lives in the Proxmark3 RDV4 it clips onto, which is already tracked separately in this database. What it actually buys you is a name for something the RDV4 could technically do already via its onboard SPI flash and standalone-mode firmware: run away from a laptop. Without this (or an equivalent Proxmark5 wireless module) the RDV4's ~40 standalone modes are a checkbox feature nobody can use in the field. Bluetooth 2.0 EDR at 4dBm/~6m range is dated compared to BLE, and the module is a genuine RDV4-specific fit - it will not clip onto a Proxmark3 Easy or a Proxmark 5, which use different connectors and wireless standards entirely (the Proxmark 5's equivalent module is a separate SKU in this same batch).",
