  "honest_take": "The performance-marketing language here ('7-8x faster image processing', 'nearly double the performance') is standard ESP32-S3-vs-S2 chip-spec talk dressed up as a product achievement - it is true of any board that swaps an S2 for an S3, not something Retia specifically engineered. The genuinely new thing is native BLE, which the older Wi-Fi/USB Nuggets did not have, and the publicly demoed BLE pairing-popup spam is a real, if by now well-worn, iOS/Android nuisance attack rather than anything novel. Whether this firmware is open source the way the original WiFi Nugget was is not stated anywhere on the product page, and no dedicated GitHub repo for this specific board was found - worth confirming before assuming it can be audited or forked.",
