  "honest_take": "The 'FPGA samples the bus, FX2LP handles the buffered high-speed USB uplink' architecture is the standard pattern for this whole product category (the same split used by the open-source Taradov design and OpenVizsla) - BugBlat just never names the actual FPGA part in any public material, so you're trusting a closed design for the part that actually does the sampling. The genuinely open piece is the host-side Python/Lua/C++ capture API on GitHub (MIT), not the gateware. At $99.99 direct it's a fair price for a real LS/FS/HS sniffer with meaningful buffer depth; paying lab401's $160-195 for the identical board is paying a real premium for UK/EU stock convenience.",
