   "notes": "Owning and using the default lock/shutdown triggers is legal everywhere the authors are aware of. Deliberately destroying data that is under a legal hold, subpoena, or active investigation — via the optional LUKS self-destruct or any other means — can be a separate criminal offense (e.g. obstruction of justice or evidence spoliation) independent of the underlying data's content, and that exposure depends heavily on jurisdiction, timing, and intent. This is not legal advice and does not describe how to avoid that exposure — check your local law and consult a lawyer if this matters to you."
