   "notes": "Building and owning the board is generally legal; several of its headline functions are not. In the United States the FCC treats intentional jammers as illegal to market, sell or operate under 47 U.S.C. 302a and 333, with no exception for private individuals, and has applied the same reasoning to Wi-Fi deauthentication - Marriott paid a $600,000 consent decree in 2014 for deauthing guest hotspots. Transmitting on sub-GHz bands without a licence, and injecting keystrokes into someone else's wireless keyboard, are separate offences in most countries. Check your local law; this is a description, not legal advice."
