  "firmware_note": "Ships with nothing pre-loaded (per the listing). You flash one of two things onto the onboard ESP32-S3 yourself: the minimal official 'mayhem-mdk' reference firmware (portapack-mayhem/mayhem-mdk), whose only documented app is a UART passthrough viewer for pin 14, or htotoo's more feature-complete third-party ESP32-Portapack firmware, which adds a Wi-Fi SSID-spam/spoofer app, an experimental IR receiver, a Meshtastic-related bridge, and an I2C link to the PortaPack. Either way, the PortaPack side also needs a Mayhem firmware build that includes the external-module API (merged via mayhem-firmware PR #2290) for any module app to appear in the Utilities menu at all - older Mayhem builds and the original 'havoc' fork predate that API and won't show the app. htotoo/ESP32-Portapack (community) or the official mayhem-mdk demo firmware",
