  "honest_take": "The single most important thing to know before buying: as sold, for $48-78, you get a PCB and a strap. Zero MCU, zero radios, zero screen - nothing that transmits, receives, or even boots on its own. It becomes a Flipper-style Wi-Fi/BT/sub-GHz/NRF24/GPS multitool only after you separately source and wire in a ~$15 CYD board, a ~$5-10 CC1101 module, a ~$5-10 amplified NRF24L01 module, and a ~$10 GPS module - none of which are in this box. If you want the finished tool, the vendor's own 'PRO' kit bundles all of that (plus a case) for $185, which is the realistic all-in price of a working Fire Weasel; this listing is for people who already own the modules (e.g. from a previous CYD build) and just want a proper carrier board and strap instead of a breadboard. Whether that convenience is worth $48-78 for a two-part PCB+strap is a judgment call - there's no independent BOM/cost breakdown published to weigh it against.",
