   "notes": "A board that can transmit on sub-GHz, 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi and 2.4 GHz nRF24 concurrently is several separate regulatory questions at once. Deauth against networks you do not own is a computer-misuse offence and an FCC interference issue in the US. Amplified nRF24 output at 500 mW exceeds what most ISM-band rules permit for that class of device in the EU and is well outside the assumptions the chip's certification was built on. Sub-GHz TX at 433 or 915 MHz has its own regional limits. Own it freely; get written authorisation before transmitting anything."
