  "honest_take": "Its identity is genuinely blurry and that is the main thing to understand before buying. It is not the best UART adapter (Tigard is cheaper and better labelled), not the best logic analyser (Glasgow, or a $10 dedicated one), and not the best USB analyser (Cynthion, from the same vendor). What it is best at is being the one board that can do a bit of everything from Python, and being solid Facedancer hardware for USB device emulation. If you have a specific problem, a specific tool beats it; if you do not yet know what your problem is, it is a reasonable thing to own.",
