  "legal": {
   "import_restricted": [],
   "risk_level": "medium",
   "notes": "Owning it would be legal in most places. The deauther, the captive portal and sub-GHz transmission are the parts that carry risk: deauthenticating networks you do not own and transmitting on licensed sub-GHz bands are separate offences in most countries, and in the United States the FCC has fined businesses specifically for Wi-Fi deauthentication. LoRa and sub-GHz band allocations differ sharply by region - 868MHz in Europe and 915MHz in the Americas are not interchangeable. Check your local law."
  },
