    "note": "SAY WHAT IT MATCHES ON: nothing. It detects the presence of an active 13.56 MHz reader field and flashes a red LED. There is no signature list, no MAC or UID matching, no protocol fingerprinting and no way to tell a hostile reader from a shop's payment terminal or a building's door reader. Treat it as an RF-field presence indicator, which is what it is."
