   "risk_level": "medium",
   "notes": "Owning it is legal in most places, and being an open-hardware development board rather than a branded consumer gadget has so far kept it clear of the import trouble the Flipper Zero has run into. That is not a guarantee: what it does is what a Flipper does, so transmitting on sub-GHz without a licence, cloning access credentials you do not own, and BadUSB against machines you do not control are all separate offences in most countries. Rainwalker OU states it is not affiliated with Flipper Zero Devices. Check your local law."
