  "honest_take": "This is the value argument for the whole scene in one product: the same ESP32-C5 dual-band radio the $220 Banshee and the ~$152 ZeroTrace AirLeak Pro are built around, running the identical free GhostESP firmware, for $12.58. What you give up is real and worth taking seriously - no battery, no buttons, no proper case, a 0.96-inch screen that is genuinely unpleasant to navigate a menu on, and no sub-GHz, NFC or IR at all. It also looks exactly like a USB flash drive without being one: the C5's USB is a Serial/JTAG peripheral, not the S3's USB-OTG, so it cannot pretend to be a keyboard. This is not a BadUSB.",
