  "status": "available",
  "released": "2023",
  "price_usd": 42.98,
  "price_note": "$42.98 for the base silver 868MHz SKU from LilyGO's China warehouse; the 'gun colour' finish is $43.99 and EU/US warehouses are about $48. The T-Watch S3 Plus at $58.74 differs only by adding GPS and a larger 940mAh battery. All SKUs include a LoRa radio USB Army Knife does not currently use.",
  "price_is_estimate": false,
  "price_checked": "2026-09-06",
  "skill_level": "advanced",
  "skill_note": "The README notes flashing this platform is more complex than the others and points to a device-specific wiki page.",
  "build_effort": "flash-only",
  "build_note": "Flash the LILYGO-T-Watch-S3 target using the project's dedicated install instructions. No soldering, but the process is fiddlier than the dongles.",
  "stealth": "covert",
  "form_factor": "wearable",
  "summary": "An ESP32-S3 smartwatch with a 240x240 touch display, 8MB PSRAM, a LoRa transceiver, microphone, accelerometer, RTC, IR emitter and haptics, running USB Army Knife. It is a wrist-worn HID injection and Wi-Fi attack platform that looks like a chunky smartwatch.",
  "honest_take": "Wearing your attack platform is the appeal and it genuinely works, but be clear on the compromises. There is no SD card slot at all, so USB Army Knife caps scripts and results at around 10MB of onboard flash - the covert-storage and long-PCAP use cases are gone. It charges and programs over Micro-USB, not USB-C, which in 2026 is an awkward thing to be carrying. Every GPIO in LilyGO's pin map is marked unavailable, so it is a sealed appliance with no expansion. And the LoRa SX1262 - the most interesting radio in this batch, and the only sub-GHz hardware anywhere in it - is not used by USB Army Knife at all, so you are paying for silicon that sits idle. Also note LilyGO's own documentation contradicts itself on the screen size, giving both 1.54 and 1.3 inches. The Wi-Fi attacks it inherits from the embedded Marauder fork have the usual ceiling too: 802.11w/PMF defeats deauth and WPA3 makes PMF mandatory.",
  "best_for": [
   "Carrying a HID injection platform somewhere a USB stick would be searched",
   "Wi-Fi and BLE recon without holding anything",
   "People who will later write their own firmware to use the LoRa radio"
  ],
  "not_for": [
   "Storage-hungry work - no SD card, roughly 10MB total",
   "Using the LoRa radio under USB Army Knife - it is unsupported",
   "Expansion of any kind - no usable GPIO",
   "Anyone who has moved on from Micro-USB"
  ],
