  "honest_take": "This is a development platform that happens to be usable for security work, not a security tool. Its two genuine advantages over a HackRF are that it is full duplex and 12-bit, which matter enormously if you are implementing a protocol that must respond to what it hears - a HackRF simply cannot do that. Against it: narrower coverage (3.5 GHz vs 6 GHz), a much smaller community, a rougher software story around LimeSuite, and a price that buys a HackRF Pro with change. Unless you specifically need full duplex or FPGA access, most people are better served elsewhere.",
