   "notes": "The LoRa radio itself operates in license-exempt 868/915 MHz ISM allocations and is low-risk if kept within regional power/duty-cycle limits (ETSI EN 300 220 / FCC Part 15) - at the module's maximum +20 dBm output you are close to or at the legal limit in some regions, so check your local allocation before maxing out power. Separately, using the LoRa link to remotely trigger a BadUSB keystroke-injection payload on a computer you do not own or lack authorization to test is a computer-crime offense independent of anything about the radio."
