   "notes": "HID injection into a machine you are not authorised to use is unauthorised access under computer-misuse law in most countries. The microphone raises a distinct and often heavier issue: covertly recording audio of people is regulated separately from computer crime, and in many US states and most of Europe recording without the consent of the parties is itself an offence, with no research exemption. Only use under written authorisation, and treat the audio capability as needing its own explicit permission. Check your local law."
