   "notes": "Owning and flashing this is legal in the US and most places. Deauth, beacon spam and Wi-Fi scanning fall into the same grey zone as any ESP32 pentest tool - illegal to point at networks you don't control in most jurisdictions. The captive-portal credential capture and rogue-DHCP/DNS features go a step further: harvesting other people's login credentials or hijacking their DNS without consent is straightforwardly a computer-misuse offence almost everywhere, not a licensing technicality. Check your local law."
