  "honest_take": "Functionally this is an RTL-SDR Blog V3-class dongle (single-input R860/R820T2 tuner, direct-sampling HF, no dedicated upconverter) in a nicer aluminum shell with USB-C instead of micro-USB - not a new design. At $49.50 it costs $10-15 more than a bare RTL-SDR Blog V3, which has the identical TCXO-and-bias-tee feature set; the premium buys the case and connector, not better reception. Community documentation, tutorials and troubleshooting all assume the RTL-SDR Blog boards, so a first-timer following any RTL-SDR guide will be working slightly off-script with this one.",
