  "honest_take": "This is instrumentation, not an attack tool by itself, and there is no capability key in this database's schema for 'passive power/EM side-channel sensing probe' - that gap is itself worth noting, since it means this device's actual function doesn't show up anywhere in the comparison table below. The differential and H-field probes measure power draw and EM emissions, which only becomes a side-channel attack once fed into capture and analysis software (ChipWhisperer or your own scope + DPA/CPA toolchain) and correlated against known plaintext/ciphertext. The isolated power supply is the unglamorous but important part: NewAE's own documentation notes the differential probe's supply rails must sit at least 2V above/below the common-mode voltage, and without galvanic isolation, ground loops between your target and your scope can swamp exactly the small signals these probes are trying to measure.",
