  "form_factor": "handheld",
  "summary": "A handheld device that couples roughly 1600 V pulses into an RFID tag or reader coil by induction, either to destroy tags permanently or to fuzz access-control readers by hitting them with electrical stress and watching how they fail. Covers LF 125-134 kHz and HF 13.56 MHz at 0-6 cm; UHF needs the separate UHFKill.",
  "honest_take": "Two very different uses get marketed as one. As a tag-killer it works and is irreversible - that is destruction of property if the badge is not yours. As a 'fuzzer' it is crude: you are inducing electrical faults and observing whether a reader fails open, reboots or corrupts, which is a legitimate but narrow test, not protocol fuzzing. At USD 299 it is expensive for what it is, it has been persistently out of stock, and it does nothing at all to read, clone or analyse cards.",
