  "summary": "An open-hardware ESP32-S3 (Waveshare ESP32-S3 Zero) + Semtech SX1262 (Seeed WIO-SX1262 module) LoRa mesh node running Meshtastic, Meshcore or Reticulum firmware, with a BMP280 environmental sensor and a Flipper-Zero-compatible pinout that lets it mount directly onto a Flipper Zero, using the Flipper as a battery and keyboard.",
  "honest_take": "This is not a Flipper Zero add-on in the GPIO-shield sense (like Electronic Cats' board) - it is an independent, fully open-source LoRa mesh node (design credited to Kody Kinzie, Zac Beran and Felix Orozco, released as open hardware at HOPE 2025) that happens to be pin-compatible with a Flipper Zero and can use it as a battery/keyboard when mounted. The underlying ESP32-S3 + SX1262 combination is a commodity Meshtastic pairing used by many boards; the $75 kit price buys Retia's case, BMP280 sensor, the dedicated 3.3V regulator fix, and convenience - not anything electrically unique, and since the full design is open-source on GitHub you can build the bare board yourself for materially less if you don't need the finished kit. If you don't specifically want the Flipper integration, a bare Heltec or LilyGo LoRa32 board running the same open Meshtastic firmware is cheaper still.",
