  "summary": "A $10 USB dongle carrying Nordic's nRF52840 SoC that, flashed with Nordic's free nRF Sniffer firmware, becomes a working BLE packet capture device feeding Wireshark. It is the cheapest legitimate way to start looking at Bluetooth Low Energy traffic.",
  "honest_take": "First, a correction that trips people up constantly: this dongle does NOT run Sniffle. Sniffle is NCC Group's sniffer and it targets TI CC1352/CC26x2 hardware only - the nRF52840 is not in its supported list and is not mentioned in the project at all. What the Nordic dongle runs is Nordic's own nRF Sniffer, which is a decent free tool but weaker: it watches one advertising channel at a time, so it frequently misses the CONNECT_IND that starts a session and therefore fails to follow the connection you actually care about. If BLE sniffing is the point of your purchase, spend $20 on a Sonoff CC2652P dongle and run Sniffle instead. Buy this one because it is a superb $10 nRF52840 development board that happens to sniff.",
