  "legal": {
   "import_restricted": [],
   "risk_level": "high",
   "notes": "The scanner and analyser modes are passive and fine. The jammer, BLE jammer and Proto Kill modes are not: operating jamming equipment is prohibited in the US under 47 U.S.C. 302a and 333 with no exemption for individuals, and under the UK Wireless Telegraphy Act 2006 and EU national equivalents. Wi-Fi deauthentication has been treated by the FCC as illegal interference (Marriott, $600,000, 2014). Interference is indiscriminate - it will hit devices belonging to people who did not consent. Check your local law; this is not legal advice."
  },
