  "legal": {
   "import_restricted": [],
   "risk_level": "high",
   "notes": "This is the most legally exposed device in the whole Hak5 catalogue, because deception is the entire product. A cable engineered to be indistinguishable from an ordinary one, that injects commands and logs keystrokes, is very difficult to characterise as anything other than deliberate unauthorised access and interception. In many jurisdictions, disguise is treated as evidence of intent and some countries have specific offences for possessing or supplying devices designed for unauthorised access. Only use with explicit written authorisation naming the machines, keep tight inventory control so a cable is never left behind, and check your local law - the possession question is genuinely different here from a Rubber Ducky."
  },
