  "stealth": "discreet",
  "form_factor": "box",
  "summary": "comma.ai's open-hardware USB CAN interface, currently sold as a single SKU ('red panda') built on an STM32H725 (4x the CPU of prior generations) with CAN-FD support on all 3 of its CAN buses plus one additional multiplexed bus. It is comma's own tool for both openpilot (where a red panda is required to run CAN-FD-only cars on a comma 3) and general car-hacking/diagnostics via its Python library and the opendbc/cabana ecosystem, and works as a plain CAN-to-USB adapter independent of openpilot.",
  "honest_take": "The '3 CAN buses, all CAN-FD' spec reads like a lab-grade interface, but comma has never published a galvanic-isolation claim anywhere in its documentation - assume it is NOT isolated between the vehicle bus and your USB port unless you find evidence otherwise, unlike CANable Pro or the (discontinued) CANtact Pro, which both market isolation as a headline feature. The real product here is the safety-audited opendbc firmware and the openpilot/cabana software ecosystem around it, not exotic hardware - at $99 it undercuts every isolated competitor, but you're trading isolation and a shipped enclosure design for that price and for openpilot integration most car-hacking buyers won't use.",
