  "name": "PicoGlitcher v3",
  "firmware": "Findus",
  "firmware_kind": "stock",
  "firmware_repo": "https://github.com/MKesenheimer/fault-injection-library",
  "firmware_note": "MicroPython-based control firmware runs on the onboard Raspberry Pi Pico 2; a companion Python host library called Findus (same repo) runs on your PC to configure glitch timing/voltage and log results. The same Findus library can also drive a ChipWhisperer Pro or Husky as an alternate capture/glitch front-end instead of this board. Findus (fault-injection-library)",
  "vendor": "Faulty Hardware (Mathias Kesenheimer)",
