  "honest_take": "The 'Killer' branding oversells it: this isn't breaking anything a PN532 or Chameleon Ultra can't already do, it's a competing implementation on a chip with no independently verifiable datasheet, so the vendor's own performance claims (4x the frame-delay speed of a Chameleon Ultra) can't be checked against a public spec. As of this research pass, the vendor's own documentation lists Darkside and StaticNested key-recovery, plus full relay attack, as 'coming soon' - not shipping - so don't assume that column is live without checking the current firmware changelog. At $29.99 it's Chameleon Ultra money for hardware with far less public scrutiny and no case included.",
