  "firmware_note": "No firmware of its own - it's a passive ISO 7816 contact slot. Functionality (e.g. `hf iclass sam`, `hf iclass tagsim`) lives entirely in the host Proxmark3's RRG/Iceman firmware, tracked separately as the base 'Proxmark3 RDV4.01' entry.",
  "vendor": "RRG (RFID Research Group) / Proxgrind - designers and manufacturers of the Proxmark3 RDV4 platform",
  "vendor_url": "https://proxmark.com",
  "product_url": "https://lab401.com/products/proxmark-3-rdv4-sim-sam-extension",
  "category": "rfid-nfc",
  "subcategory": "Proxmark3 RDV4 accessory: SIM/SAM smart-card slot extension",
  "status": "available",
  "released": null,
  "price_usd": 26.0,
  "price_note": "Confirmed $26.00 directly on Lab401's USD storefront (€19.95 on their EUR storefront). Sold standalone for owners of earlier RDV4.0 units; RRG has bundled this extension with every RDV4.01 sold since 2021, so RDV4.01 buyers already have it.",
  "price_is_estimate": false,
  "price_checked": "2026-09-10",
  "skill_level": "advanced",
  "skill_note": "Only useful to someone already running Proxmark3/RRG firmware and pursuing SAM-based research (e.g. HID iCLASS PACS/SIO decode) - not a beginner accessory, and a genuine HID SAM is not something a hobbyist can easily or legitimately obtain.",
  "build_effort": "assembled",
  "build_note": "Plug-in module onto the RDV4 mainboard's dedicated SIM/SAM header - no soldering.",
  "stealth": "discreet",
  "form_factor": "board",
  "summary": "A small extension module that plugs into the dedicated SIM/SAM header on a Proxmark 3 RDV4 or RDV4.01 mainboard, exposing a full-size ISO 7816 contact smart-card slot. It enables the Proxmark's RRG/Iceman firmware to interface with a real SIM- or SAM-format smart card for contact-chip operations the Proxmark's contactless RF frontend cannot do alone - for example, the documented `hf iclass sam` command uses a genuine HID SAM inserted here to extract PACS data from an iCLASS card dump. It has no RF/RFID capability of its own - it is purely a contact-interface accessory.",
  "honest_take": "This does nothing by itself and requires a Proxmark 3 RDV4/RDV4.01 host - it's purely an accessory, already tracked as bundled-in on the base RDV4.01 entry in this database, so only buy it separately if you have an older RDV4.0 without one. The bigger catch isn't the module (a cheap, simple contact-slot board) but what you put in it: a genuine HID SAM is not something sold to the general public, so most buyers will own the slot and never have a legitimate card to put in it - the module's real value is narrow and specific to researchers who already have vetted SAM access. Every RFID/NFC capability key below is 'no' for this exact reason: it has zero contactless capability, that all belongs to the host RDV4.",
