  "price_note": "ESTIMATE, parts only. Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W ~$18-25 (the 32-bit Pi Zero W is now legacy - the fork dropped 32-bit images at v2.9.5.7), microSD 32GB ~$8, Waveshare 2.13in e-ink HAT ~$25-30 (this is the single biggest line item and the part beginners forget), and power. A PiSugar 3 (the project's named partner) is ~$40; a generic USB power bank is ~$12 but makes it a brick in your pocket rather than a wearable. Case ~$10-15 printed or bought. Realistic all-in: $65 on a power bank, $105-120 with a PiSugar. You do NOT need a USB Wi-Fi adapter - see the honest take.",
