   "notes": "The monitoring, inventory and threat-intel features are benign. The offensive functions inherited from Bjorn - credential brute-forcing and file extraction - are not, and running them against systems you do not own is unauthorised access under the CFAA in the US, the Computer Misuse Act in the UK and equivalents elsewhere. Because it also fetches from external threat-intelligence services, consider what its outbound traffic reveals about the network it is sitting on. Check your local law; this is not legal advice."
