  "stealth": "discreet",
  "form_factor": "pocket",
  "summary": "Free open-source software that turns a cheap LTE hotspot into a cell-site-simulator (IMSI catcher / stingray) detector by reading the Qualcomm modem's diagnostic interface and applying heuristics for things like downgrade attempts and unusual identity requests. Roughly nine hotspot models are supported, with the Orbic RC400L the reference device in the Americas.",
  "honest_take": "It detects behaviour consistent with a cell-site simulator; it cannot prove one is present, and a quiet or well-configured catcher can go unflagged. It watches only the band and carrier the hotspot is attached to, so it is a sampling instrument, not a shield - it does not protect your phone, it tells you the airspace looked wrong. The hardware side is a used consumer hotspot, so battery health and firmware build vary and behaviour genuinely differs between units.",
  "best_for": [
   "Journalists, activists and researchers documenting surveillance at protests or borders",
   "Cheap, legal, passive cellular monitoring",
   "Contributing real-world data to a public research effort"
  ],
