   "risk_level": "high",
   "notes": "Covertly recording what appears on someone else's screen is squarely the kind of surveillance that interception, wiretap and privacy statutes are written about, and in many jurisdictions it is treated more seriously than network sniffing because of what screens display - medical records, messages, banking. Several US states and many other countries also have specific laws about recording in private spaces. This is a device you should only deploy with explicit written authorisation naming the specific machines involved."
