  "honest_take": "SparkFun's own GitHub README describes this in one sentence: it lets you 'view SPI signals between an SD socket and SD card' - so despite a full-size SD card physically carrying DAT1-DAT3 lines for 4-bit SDIO mode, the board and its documentation are built and described around SPI-mode sniffing. If your target host talks to the card in 4-bit mode (many cameras and higher-throughput embedded hosts do), you're on your own for decoding those extra lines even though the pins may be physically present on the header. Functionally identical value proposition to the microSD Sniffer, just for full-size cards, and it shares the same complete absence of debug-port, I2C or glitching capability.",
