  "honest_take": "There is no evidence Hacker Warehouse designed or builds this - the SKU (EC-WMFZ), the ESP32-S3 spec, and the product description text all match Electronic Cats' own $40 Marauder add-on word for word, and Hacker Warehouse is charging $10 more for the identical board. Unless you specifically want it bundled with Hacker Warehouse's other gear or shipping, buy direct from Electronic Cats and save $10. Beyond that, this is the same story as every Marauder board: it's a WiFi/BLE scanner and spammer, not a Flipper-native capability, deauth dies against any WPA3/PMF network, and it has no screen, battery, GPS or confirmed onboard SD of its own - it is entirely dependent on the Flipper for power, display and storage.",
