  "legal": {
   "import_restricted": [],
   "risk_level": "high",
   "notes": "Receiving on sub-GHz is generally lawful. Transmitting is where the risk is: the device's ranges cover licensed land-mobile, amateur, paging and public-safety allocations as well as licence-exempt ISM bands, and transmitting outside the ISM allocations without a licence is an offence in most countries. Separately, transmitting to actuate a gate, garage, alarm or vehicle you do not own is typically a criminal offence in its own right regardless of frequency. Check your local regulator's ISM band plan before transmitting."
  },
